  "result": "If I could change the world in just one way, I\u2019d give every person a genuine, effortless capacity for empathy\u2014an innate ability to see, feel and understand the lives of others (human and non-human alike). \n\nWhy?  \n\u2022 Conflict and violence often stem from fear and misunderstanding. If we all truly felt the joys and sufferings of people halfway across the globe\u2014or the pain of a displaced animal\u2014we\u2019d be far less willing to harm or ignore them.  \n\u2022 Many of our greatest challenges\u2014poverty, injustice, environmental collapse\u2014arise because short-term self-interest trumps concern for those who come after us. Empathy rewires us toward long-term, collective well-being.  \n\u2022 Empathy fuels cooperation, creativity and innovation. When we care as deeply about our neighbors (and our planet) as we do about ourselves, we unlock solutions we\u2019d never imagine in a world driven by competition and indifference.\n\nWith universal empathy as our baseline, borders soften, resource-sharing becomes natural, and policies\u2014social, economic, environmental\u2014are designed to sustain life rather than exploit it. In that one shift, nearly every global problem takes on a new, solvable shape.",
